      "next_deadline": "Funds may be requested through the annual Affordable Housing Development NOFO or by direct approach to ComDev; the County reported that no developer had taken on HOME-ARP in the three years before Sendero Commons, so the remaining balance is effectively available to the next PSH project that can navigate the federal requirements.",
      "prevailing_wage_trigger": "true",
      "layering_notes": "Fresno County splits housing work three ways: the Department of Public Works and Planning, Community Development Division (ComDev) runs the Urban County HUD programs, PLHA and the annual Affordable Housing Development NOFO; the County Administrative Office's new Office of Housing and Homelessness (OHH, created November 18, 2025) administers HHAP, the Continuum of Care and Transitional Rent and is absorbing housing programs from Behavioral Health and ComDev (Phase 2 approved November 3, 2026); and the Department of Behavioral Health co-applies for Homekey+ and NPLH and funds BHSA housing. Fresno Housing (the joint City and County Housing Authorities) is the dominant developer and voucher source. The City of Fresno and Clovis are separate entitlements with their own programs (Pass 3). fresnocountyca.gov and fresnohousing.org open normally; Board records are on fresnocounty.legistar.com and the Legistar web API client 'fresnocounty'. HOME-ARP is being used as the County's capital piece in the Sendero Commons stack (Homekey+, NPLH, HHIP and PLHA). Staff flagged the program's complexity and a hard 2030 expenditure deadline, so a shovel-ready PSH project in a JPA city or unincorporated area could pick up any unspent balance quickly. Source is the October 20, 2026 Board item (file 26-0945) with the draft amended Allocation Plan.",
